You are helping build "Ajaia Docs", a lightweight Google Docs-style editor for a 4-6 hour take-home assessment.

Stack: Next.js (App Router), TypeScript strict, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Tiptap, Supabase (Postgres, Auth, RLS), Zod, Vitest, Vercel.

Rules:

- Build one milestone at a time. Do not implement features from later milestones.
- Keep it simple: no extra abstractions, no state libraries, no separate API layer. Use Server Actions or route handlers.
- Authorization is enforced in the database (RLS) AND validated server-side. Hiding UI is never security.
- Never expose the Supabase service role key to the client. It is only used in seed scripts.
- Validate all external input with Zod.
- After each milestone, summarize what you changed, what could break, and how to verify it.
- If you are unsure or a decision has tradeoffs, ask before choosing.
